      "title": "WalletGuard: A Crypto Phishing Campaign Hosted Entirely on GitHub",
      "summary": "A GitHub phishing campaign, dubbed WalletGuard, opened issues on over 200 cryptocurrency, wallet and developer-tool repositories in under 20 minutes on November 25, 2026. The issues falsely claimed wallet keys had leaked and urged maintainers to move funds to attacker wallets and submit seed phrases or private keys to a fake verification page. That page sent the secrets to a webhook[.]site collector, then displayed a \"no exposure found\" message to reassure victims. A companion CLI, walletguard-cli, collected wallet secrets, SSH keys and cloud credentials and exfiltrated them through a Cloudflare Worker to Telegram. Defenders should treat unsolicited \"security exposure\" issues as hostile and never provide seed phrases or private keys to third-party verification services.",
