      "report_date": "2026-11-25",
      "title": "Risk Alert: Widespread Spread of a New Variant of the Cling Remote-Access Botnet",
      "summary": "The new Cling botnet variant primarily targets Linux servers and IoT devices, and CNCERT detected its widespread propagation in November 2026. It hides command-and-control traffic among public STUN services by embedding commands in the STUN Transaction ID field, making its traffic difficult to separate from legitimate STUN exchanges. This variant removes propagation, proxying, and DDoS modules, retaining command execution and program download-and-execute capabilities to maintain long-term control of compromised hosts. Attackers use infected hosts as launchpads for delivering other malware, and the report counted about 5,600 infected devices in mainland China between November 9 and 20. Defenders are advised to monitor for anomalous STUN traffic on UDP port 3478 and non-random Transaction IDs, and to inspect startup entries in files such as /etc/inittab.",
