      "report_date": "2026-11-25",
      "title": "PolinRider Malware Force-Pushed Into AsyncAPI, CircuitVerse and Open Food Facts Pull Requests",
      "summary": "PolinRider, a malware loader, was force-pushed by the GitHub account Eternity0207 into open pull requests at AsyncAPI Generator, CircuitVerse, Open Food Facts and Jaeger, with a Jaeger branch carrying it from July to October 2026. The loader is hidden in api.js, build and test config files, and a fake font file, and it runs through build scripts, test runs, or a hidden VS Code task when a folder is opened. It fetches its server address from a public Ethereum wallet that the operator updates about every three hours. CircuitVerse's CI ran the loader and published 40 infected installers, which were deleted. Defenders should require approval for fork pull request workflows, avoid publishing artifacts from forks, and review force-pushed changes and unsigned commits.",
