      "title": "Silver Fox SEO Poisoning: How Fake Software Downloads Spread Gh0stRAT",
      "summary": "Silver Fox, a financially driven threat group also tracked as SwimSnake, distributed Gh0stRAT through a fake oCam installer promoted via SEO poisoning. The installer delivered the genuine application alongside hidden malware, and its loader adapted to whichever of three Chinese antivirus products was running. The Gh0stRAT variant used a custom loader to run its payload in memory and hide its command-and-control address. In the endpoint examined, two EDR layers stopped the attack within about 90 seconds, with cloud classification blocking the malicious DLL and behavioral detection blocking a PowerShell attempt to weaken Microsoft Defender. Defenders should treat third-party download portals as untrusted and watch for installers launching scripting engines to modify security settings.",
